.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-webhooks-event-callbacks - List delivery attempts for a webhook


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 webhooks event-callbacks  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the delivery attempts for a webhook — the log to read when a callback did
not arrive.

.PP
Each row is one attempt, with its status and the event it carried, so it
answers the two questions worth asking: is the gateway trying at all (no rows
means the event never dispatched — check that the webhook is active and the
topic matches), and if it is, what is the receiver returning.

.PP
\&'--status failed' is the usual starting point, and the one to read before
\&'reset-circuit'; '--response-code 500' then tells the receiver's crashes apart
from its rate limits. '--payment-id' narrows to one payment, named by either
its UUID or its 0x rail0_id — any payment of the account, whichever of its
wallets it belongs to. The gateway keeps 15 days of attempts; page through them
with --page / --per-page.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for event-callbacks

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--payment-id\fP=""
	Filter by the payment the delivery is for: its UUID or its 0x rail0_id

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Attempts per page

.PP
\fB--response-code\fP=""
	Filter by the receiver's exact HTTP response code (e.g. 500)

.PP
\fB--since\fP=""
	Only deliveries at/after this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort fields (e.g. -created_at)

.PP
\fB--status\fP=""
	Filter by delivery status ('delivered', 'failed')

.PP
\fB--topic\fP=""
	Filter by event topic (e.g. payments.captured)

.PP
\fB--until\fP=""
	Only deliveries at/before this ISO-8601 time


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 webhooks event-callbacks whk_abc123 --status failed
  rail0 webhooks event-callbacks whk_abc123 --topic payments.captured
  rail0 webhooks event-callbacks whk_abc123 --status failed --response-code 500
  rail0 webhooks event-callbacks whk_abc123 --payment-id 0x… --since 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-webhooks(1)\fP
